<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Buying]]></title>
  <link>https://example.com/buying/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">https://example.com/buying/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:html -->
<article class="prose-page" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><header class="prose-head" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p class="pretitle" data-reveal data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Buying</p><h1 class="h-big" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Buying a home on the islands</h1><p class="lead prose-lead" data-reveal style="--delay:.2s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Island houses are bought on ferry time. Here is how a purchase goes, and what to check that a mainland buyer might miss.</p></header><img class="prose-img" src="/wp-content/themes/shoal/assets/img/tile-living.webp" alt="A living room with a stone fireplace and glass doors open to a deck over the bay" width="1920" height="1072" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><div class="prose-body" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><h2>How a purchase goes</h2><ol><li><strong>A first call.</strong> Which island, how you will live there, and what you want to spend. Twenty minutes.</li><li><strong>A viewing day.</strong> Four to six houses planned around the ferry schedule, with lunch in Teal Harbor.</li><li><strong>The offer.</strong> Island sales usually include well, septic and bluff inspections as conditions. Dana writes them in.</li><li><strong>Inspections and closing.</strong> Thirty to forty-five days, with the inspectors booked the day the offer is accepted.</li></ol><h2>What to inspect</h2><p>Wells, septic systems, bluffs and anything metal near salt water. Ask for the well flow test and a water quality report, a septic inspection with a pump-out, and a geotechnical report for any home near a bank.</p><h2 id="second-homes">Second homes</h2><p>About a third of island homes are second homes. If you plan to rent yours out in summer, check the island's short-term rental rules before you make an offer, and budget for a caretaker who checks the house after winter storms.</p><button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Plan a viewing day</button></div></article>
<!-- /wp:html -->]]></content:encoded>
