  <guid isPermaLink="false">https://example.com/areas/teal-harbor/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:html -->
<article class="prose-page" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><header class="prose-head" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p class="pretitle" data-reveal data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Island guide</p><h1 class="h-big" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Teal Harbor</h1><p class="lead prose-lead" data-reveal style="--delay:.2s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>The island town: school, clinic and the busiest ferry dock.</p></header><img class="prose-img" src="/wp-content/themes/shoal/assets/img/area-harbor.webp" alt="Sailboats and motor yachts in a calm marina at dusk" width="1920" height="1072" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><div class="prose-body" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p>Teal Harbor is where the islands do their errands. The marina, the clinic, the K–8 school and the Saturday market are all within a ten-minute walk of the ferry dock.</p><p>Most homes are 1920s cottages and 1990s family houses on small lots. Waterfront here usually means a view across the marina rather than a private beach.</p><p>Buyers who work on the mainland like it because the first ferry leaves at 5:40 and the walk from the door to the dock is short.</p><dl><dt>Ferry to the mainland</dt><dd>35 minutes</dd><dt>Typical home</dt><dd>3-bed cottage on a 5,000 sq ft lot</dd><dt>Good for</dt><dd>Year-round living, families, commuters</dd></dl><button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Ask about Teal Harbor</button></div></article>
<!-- /wp:html -->]]></content:encoded>
