<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Brannock Island]]></title>
  <link>https://example.com/areas/brannock-island/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">https://example.com/areas/brannock-island/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:html -->
<article class="prose-page" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><header class="prose-head" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p class="pretitle" data-reveal data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Island guide</p><h1 class="h-big" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Brannock Island</h1><p class="lead prose-lead" data-reveal style="--delay:.2s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Forest, farms and long gravel roads. Quiet all winter.</p></header><img class="prose-img" src="/wp-content/themes/shoal/assets/img/area-ferry.webp" alt="A ferry entering the harbour between two stone breakwaters" width="1920" height="1072" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><div class="prose-body" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p>Brannock is the biggest island and the least built up. Many properties are five acres or more, with wells and septic systems, so inspections matter more than the listing photos.</p><p>The north shore has the sunsets and the steep driveways. The south end has the farms, the flat land and the best soil for a garden.</p><p>Internet is good along the main road and patchy in the hills. Ask for a speed test before you fall in love with a view.</p><dl><dt>Ferry to the mainland</dt><dd>50 minutes</dd><dt>Typical home</dt><dd>Farmhouse or cabin on 5+ acres</dd><dt>Good for</dt><dd>Space, gardens, working from home</dd></dl><button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Ask about Brannock Island</button></div></article>
<!-- /wp:html -->]]></content:encoded>
