<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Larkspur Point]]></title>
  <link>https://example.com/areas/larkspur-point/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">https://example.com/areas/larkspur-point/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:html -->
<article class="prose-page" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><header class="prose-head" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p class="pretitle" data-reveal data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Island guide</p><h1 class="h-big" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Larkspur Point</h1><p class="lead prose-lead" data-reveal style="--delay:.2s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>The lighthouse, rocky shore and the deepest moorage.</p></header><img class="prose-img" src="/wp-content/themes/shoal/assets/img/area-lighthouse.webp" alt="A red and white lighthouse on a cliff above the sea" width="1920" height="1072" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><div class="prose-body" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p>Larkspur Point is a peninsula at the south end of Fennick Island, joined to it by a single causeway. Its rocky shore and deep water make it the place for boat owners.</p><p>Homes are few and change hands rarely. Most sales happen before they are listed, so tell me early if this is the place you want.</p><p>Wind is part of the deal. Houses here are built low, with storm shutters, and the gardens are grass and rock.</p><dl><dt>Ferry to the mainland</dt><dd>45 minutes via Fennick</dd><dt>Typical home</dt><dd>Waterfront house with deep-water moorage</dd><dt>Good for</dt><dd>Boat owners, people who like weather</dd></dl><button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Ask about Larkspur Point</button></div></article>
<!-- /wp:html -->]]></content:encoded>
