<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Fennick Island]]></title>
  <link>https://example.com/areas/fennick-island/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">https://example.com/areas/fennick-island/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:html -->
<article class="prose-page" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><header class="prose-head" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p class="pretitle" data-reveal data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Island guide</p><h1 class="h-big" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Fennick Island</h1><p class="lead prose-lead" data-reveal style="--delay:.2s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Sea thrift on the bluffs, pebble beaches, open water.</p></header><img class="prose-img" src="/wp-content/themes/shoal/assets/img/area-meadow.webp" alt="Pink sea thrift on a cliff above the ocean" width="1920" height="1072" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><div class="prose-body" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p>Fennick faces east, towards the mountains, and its bluffs are covered in wildflowers from May to July. Many homes here are second homes that the owners let in summer.</p><p>The bluffs are beautiful and they move. Before buying near the edge, read the geotechnical report and ask how far the bank has retreated in the last twenty years.</p><p>Beach access is public at four points, so a home a street back from the water often costs half as much and loses little.</p><dl><dt>Ferry to the mainland</dt><dd>40 minutes</dd><dt>Typical home</dt><dd>Bluff-top house or beach cabin</dd><dt>Good for</dt><dd>Second homes, summer rentals, retirement</dd></dl><button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Ask about Fennick Island</button></div></article>
<!-- /wp:html -->]]></content:encoded>
